  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse d&apos;urgence en pr&#xe9;vention, prise en charge des Violences Bas&#xe9;es sur le Genre (VBG) et protection contre l&#x2019;exploitation et les abus sexuels dans les provinces de l&apos;Ituri, Nord-Kivu, Sud- Kivu, Kasa&#xef;, Kasa&#xef; Central et Tanganyika</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving gender-based violence protection assistance to internally displaced persons, returnees and host community members in Ituri, Kasa&#xef;, Kasa&#xef;-Central, North Kivu, South Kivu and Tanganyika provinces. This UNFPA project provides GBV psycho-social support and case management services; provides medical care to survivors of gender-based violence; provides essential sexual and reproductive healthcare supplies to 24 health centres; trains healthcare workers on the clinical management of rape; raises awareness in communities about gender-based violence; establishes community mechanisms to report complaints including of sexual exploitation and abuse; establishes women- and girl-friendly safe spaces; provides cash transfers; and distributes menstrual hygiene management and dignity kits. The project provides life-saving assistance to 105,692 people, including 22,304 women, 21,589 men, 61,799 children, and 5,562 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
